# Task 143-004: API Auth Default Secure — Execution Plan

## Problem
1. `bearerAuthMiddleware` in auth.ts: `if (!activeToken) return true` — no token = auth disabled (insecure default)
2. server.ts `checkAuth`: `if (!token) return true` — same pattern
3. No CORS origin restriction (only localhost but wildcard-like)
4. No security headers (X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, CSP, HSTS)

## Approach

### 1. auth.ts Changes
- Remove `if (!activeToken) return true` from bearerAuthMiddleware
- Add `DECKENT_API_AUTH_DISABLED=1` env check: if set → return true + stderr warning
- Default: no token configured + no bypass env → 401 for all API requests

### 2. server.ts Changes
- Remove legacy `checkAuth` function (replaced by bearerAuthMiddleware)
- Remove legacy fallback block in handleRequest
- Add security headers middleware: X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, CSP, HSTS
- Tighten CORS: only allow localhost/127.0.0.1 origins (already mostly done, verify wildcard blocked)
- Add security headers to sendJson and sendError responses
- Update createHttpServer: warn on stderr when auth disabled via env bypass

### 3. Tests
- Missing token → 401 (no bypass env)
- DECKENT_API_AUTH_DISABLED=1 → pass through + stderr warning
- Valid token → 200
- Invalid token → 403
- CORS reject for non-localhost origin
- Security headers present (X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, CSP, HSTS)
- Health endpoint still exempt
- POST endpoints require auth

## Files Modified
- src/api/auth.ts — default secure + bypass env
- src/api/server.ts — remove legacy checkAuth, add security headers
- tests/api/server-auth.test.ts — update existing + add new tests
- tests/api/security-headers.test.ts — update to expect headers present
